There are a large number of task-dag tasks that are still technically open, but are being skipped by the dispatcher because an associated github issue is already closed.

We really should clean these tasks up.  Either complete-historical or complete-ops* should probably work, but may require the GH issue to be temporarily reopened (although that seems like a bug or tooling gap if so).

We should also consider how this happens, and have an automated reactive way to either complete a task or perhaps better mark it as blocked somehow if its GH issue is closed before it is resolved.

```yaml
{
  "delegated_to": [
    {
      "repo": "virusdave/task-dag",
      "issue": 12,
      "note": "Implement `reconcile-closed-issue <issue>` per top-level docs/designs/closed-issue-task-reconciliation.md §3 (operator-signed-off policy §2). Default drop-with-audit; --dry-run/--json/--yes; fail-safe (no mutation unless issue CONFIRMED CLOSED); frontier-first --force-with-lease deletes of only refs at the expected SHA; never delete tasks/pending/<N> or gh/comments provenance; leave tasks/active/* alone. Reuse drop/ref-helper/blocked --json resolution and share logic with cleanup-closed-issue-task-refs.sh. Critical infra: Oracle change review; NO ref/commit FORMAT change or new namespace (stop + get operator+Oracle approval if one becomes necessary). Tests + docs; keep offline validate offline."
    }
  ]
}
```

The agent waste log review page (https://helios.freshlybaked.us/config/agent-waste) Should give me a button that sends all of the pending reports to our more advanced bedrock LLM for clustering / matching similar reports, which clustering should then be reflected in the UI (a primary with a total count, and with a collapsed but expandable set of cluster matches).

Clusters should be sorted on that resulting page by "likely aggregate agent waste" accumulated across all near-duplicate or highly-similar reports, allowing the operator to directly address the most common or most important issues first. 

